    "result_text": "Done. All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\nI added the per-country national-number check to `NormalizeOwnerTelephone.service` \u2014 the single lowest-impact edit:\n\n- **One file touched**, and the class has only one method (WMC_other = 1), so the surrounding-complexity cost is minimal.\n- Added two guard clauses right after the existing E.164 length check:\n  - `+61` \u2192 must have 9 national digits (`count - 2`)\n  - `+1` \u2192 must have 10 national digits (`count - 1`)\n- Both throw the existing checked `InvalidTelephoneException`, which the existing handler already maps to **400**, so no new classes, escalation YAML, or wiring were needed.\n\nThe default valid payload (`04XXXXXXXX` \u2192 `+61` + 9 digits) and the `+1` NANP seed data (10 national digits) both still pass, and the new test rejecting `+61 123` returns 400.",
